70
00:02:37,786 --> 00:02:40,408
Now for the actual algorithm. How does this

71
00:02:40,602 --> 00:02:42,413
bubble sort algorithm work?

72
00:02:43,998 --> 00:02:47,361
We actually will have 2 nested for loops.

73
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,804
We'll have one outer for loop,

74
00:02:50,371 --> 00:02:52,964
which I'll simply name outer. My iteration

75
00:02:52,981 --> 00:02:55,963
variable is named outer, which starts at 0,

76
00:02:56,611 --> 00:03:00,239
and I proceed as long as outer is smaller

77
00:03:00,288 --> 00:03:01,285
than resultArray.length,

78
00:03:03,678 --> 00:03:04,122
and I

79
00:03:04,912 --> 00:03:07,197
add 1 to outer after every iteration.

80
00:03:07,878 --> 00:03:11,005
Now I'm naming this iterator variable outer

81
00:03:11,053 --> 00:03:13,490
here so that it's easy to identify inside of

82
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:14,116
the loop later.

83
00:03:15,078 --> 00:03:17,611
Because as I just said, we will also have

84
00:03:18,108 --> 00:03:20,610
another loop in there, a nested for loop,

85
00:03:21,010 --> 00:03:22,373
which I'll of course name inner.

86
00:03:23,095 --> 00:03:25,644
And that inner variable will basically be my

87
00:03:25,885 --> 00:03:27,392
outer variable plus 1.

88
00:03:28,146 --> 00:03:30,519
So for the first loop iteration of the outer

89
00:03:30,535 --> 00:03:33,662
loop, that will be 1 because outer is 0,

90
00:03:33,902 --> 00:03:35,169
outer plus 1 is 1.

91
00:03:36,227 --> 00:03:39,018
And we will continue in here as long as

92
00:03:39,275 --> 00:03:41,665
inner is smaller than result

93
00:03:42,419 --> 00:03:45,194
array.length. So that's the same condition

94
00:03:45,290 --> 00:03:46,942
as in the outer loop here.

95
00:03:47,792 --> 00:03:49,781
And just as in the outer loop, I'll

96
00:03:49,781 --> 00:03:51,241
increment inner by 1 here.

97
00:03:52,139 --> 00:03:54,368
So we got 2 nested loops here. Why do we

98
00:03:54,368 --> 00:03:56,774
need nested loops? Well, keep in mind what

99
00:03:56,774 --> 00:03:57,945
you saw on the slide

100
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:01,955
there. We in the end compare 2 values

101
00:04:02,693 --> 00:04:03,639
and we get

102
00:04:04,216 --> 00:04:07,422
through 2 values, therefore we need 2 loops.

103
00:04:07,759 --> 00:04:11,125
We change the first value and we change the

104
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:14,380
value for every first value we're comparing

105
00:04:14,428 --> 00:04:17,730
it to. So here you could say 3 is our outer

106
00:04:17,938 --> 00:04:18,307
value,

107
00:04:19,221 --> 00:04:20,936
-3 is our inner value,

108
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:24,398
and then we swap them. So now we got a new

109
00:04:24,655 --> 00:04:27,669
outer value, but still we got that outer

110
00:04:27,781 --> 00:04:30,650
position, that outer index, which still is

111
00:04:30,682 --> 00:04:34,033
0, and we're comparing that value in that

112
00:04:34,033 --> 00:04:35,539
index to all following

113
00:04:36,437 --> 00:04:39,051
values, and that's our nested loop. So now

114
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:43,413
we're comparing it to 48 and to 5 and to 33

115
00:04:43,509 --> 00:04:45,594
thereafter, and so on. So that's what we're

116
00:04:45,594 --> 00:04:46,011
doing here.

117
00:04:46,636 --> 00:04:48,609
And this item on the right, which is moving

118
00:04:48,962 --> 00:04:52,185
from 33 to 99 now, for example, that's our

119
00:04:52,313 --> 00:04:52,730
inner loop.

120
00:04:53,372 --> 00:04:56,162
Eventually that inner loop finishes once we

121
00:04:56,162 --> 00:04:59,129
compared the outer element, the first

122
00:04:59,129 --> 00:05:01,502
element here, with all our following

123
00:05:01,614 --> 00:05:04,900
elements. And then we go to that outer loop

124
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:08,826
and increment outer to 1, for example, to

125
00:05:08,826 --> 00:05:11,038
have a look at the element at index 1.

126
00:05:11,567 --> 00:05:14,323
And now again, run the nested loop for all

127
00:05:14,756 --> 00:05:17,496
our elements following that, which is why we

128
00:05:17,496 --> 00:05:20,926
have outer plus 1 as a value for inner. We

129
00:05:20,926 --> 00:05:23,682
look at the element at the next index. So

130
00:05:23,682 --> 00:05:25,846
now again, we have a swap here, but that

131
00:05:25,894 --> 00:05:28,169
doesn't impact our loops. We continue

132
00:05:28,233 --> 00:05:30,108
running through those nested loops, and now

133
00:05:30,317 --> 00:05:32,544
we go through all those elements again in

134
00:05:32,544 --> 00:05:35,350
the inner loop. Until we reach the last

135
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:35,880
element here,

136
00:05:36,954 --> 00:05:39,279
and then the inner loop is done again, and

137
00:05:39,295 --> 00:05:43,545
the outer loop increments the value to 2. So

138
00:05:43,545 --> 00:05:46,240
now we have a look at the element at index 2

139
00:05:46,656 --> 00:05:48,437
in the outer loop. So that's why we have

140
00:05:48,517 --> 00:05:52,205
nested loops, because we change 2 elements

141
00:05:52,205 --> 00:05:55,108
and we compare all elements to all other

142
00:05:55,316 --> 00:05:57,081
elements, hence the nested loops.

143
00:05:57,802 --> 00:06:00,369
Now in the outer loop Before we enter the

144
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:03,626
inner loop, we therefore define our outer

145
00:06:04,381 --> 00:06:04,750
element.

146
00:06:06,082 --> 00:06:07,975
And for that, we have a look at the copied

147
00:06:08,007 --> 00:06:08,248
array

148
00:06:09,131 --> 00:06:12,581
and get the element at index outer. So for

149
00:06:12,581 --> 00:06:14,924
the first iteration, 0. For the second

150
00:06:14,924 --> 00:06:17,540
iteration, 1. So the second element, and so

151
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:17,844
on.

152
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,696
Now inside of the inner loop, we now have

153
00:06:22,033 --> 00:06:23,846
the inner element therefore,

154
00:06:24,376 --> 00:06:27,393
and that is result array for the, you

155
00:06:27,425 --> 00:06:30,153
guessed it, inner element. So for the first

156
00:06:30,153 --> 00:06:32,303
loop iteration of the outer and the inner

157
00:06:32,303 --> 00:06:34,887
loops, for the first iteration of each loop,

158
00:06:35,272 --> 00:06:37,374
that would be the second item in the array

159
00:06:37,599 --> 00:06:40,504
because inner initially is outer, which is 0

160
00:06:40,905 --> 00:06:41,418
plus 1.

161
00:06:42,044 --> 00:06:46,040
So that's 1 overall. So the index 1 passed

162
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,335
to result array, and that's the second

163
00:06:48,511 --> 00:06:48,929
element.

164
00:06:49,635 --> 00:06:51,865
So for the first iterations, we have the

165
00:06:51,898 --> 00:06:53,743
first and the second elements here.

166
00:06:54,868 --> 00:06:57,341
And now we simply compare them. We check if

167
00:06:57,341 --> 00:06:59,476
the outer element, which is the first one,

168
00:06:59,782 --> 00:07:01,869
if that's greater than the inner element.

169
00:07:02,174 --> 00:07:04,551
And here I'm writing the algorithm to sort

170
00:07:04,647 --> 00:07:07,361
in ascending order. If you want descending

171
00:07:07,458 --> 00:07:09,320
order, you would basically revert this.

172
00:07:10,204 --> 00:07:13,014
So here I'm checking for outer L greater

173
00:07:13,014 --> 00:07:13,769
than inner L.

174
00:07:14,925 --> 00:07:15,872
If that's the case,

175
00:07:16,932 --> 00:07:19,277
if the first element in the array is bigger

176
00:07:19,277 --> 00:07:21,429
than the second element, we need to swap

177
00:07:21,429 --> 00:07:23,919
them, right? Because then we have a bigger

178
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,152
element in front of a smaller one, and for

179
00:07:26,409 --> 00:07:28,594
ascending sorting, that's the wrong order.

180
00:07:29,638 --> 00:07:31,325
So we would go to the result array,

181
00:07:32,192 --> 00:07:32,658
access

182
00:07:33,253 --> 00:07:33,413
the

183
00:07:33,976 --> 00:07:35,646
element at position outer,

184
00:07:36,305 --> 00:07:38,554
so the first element for the first

185
00:07:38,554 --> 00:07:39,164
iterations,

186
00:07:40,241 --> 00:07:42,201
and set the element that's stored in that

187
00:07:42,249 --> 00:07:44,546
position in the array equal to the inner

188
00:07:44,642 --> 00:07:44,964
element.

189
00:07:46,008 --> 00:07:48,498
And we would also go to result array for the

190
00:07:48,578 --> 00:07:51,548
element at index inner, we would set the

191
00:07:51,629 --> 00:07:52,544
outer element.

192
00:07:53,170 --> 00:07:56,285
That simply swaps these 2 elements. So if we

193
00:07:56,285 --> 00:07:58,726
have this on an array that looks like,

194
00:07:59,272 --> 00:08:00,428
let's say, this,

195
00:08:01,198 --> 00:08:02,258
the result would be

196
00:08:02,884 --> 00:08:03,093
this

197
00:08:03,928 --> 00:08:06,417
because we take the index of the outer

198
00:08:06,561 --> 00:08:08,263
element, which is 0 for the first

199
00:08:08,263 --> 00:08:10,158
iterations, so the first element,

200
00:08:10,816 --> 00:08:13,112
and replace the element there with inner l.

201
00:08:13,818 --> 00:08:16,401
So the old outerEl is replaced with innerEl,

202
00:08:16,867 --> 00:08:19,032
but we saved outerEl into a separate

203
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:21,792
variable before we did that, so we can still

204
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:25,433
use that outer element to in turn replace

205
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:27,824
the old inner element with it. So the old

206
00:08:27,824 --> 00:08:30,342
second element with the old first element

207
00:08:30,792 --> 00:08:31,706
and the other way around.

208
00:08:32,252 --> 00:08:33,294
That's what we're doing here.

209
00:08:34,578 --> 00:08:36,583
And in case you can't wrap your head around

210
00:08:36,583 --> 00:08:38,989
this, simply dump in a console.log

211
00:08:38,989 --> 00:08:41,351
thereafter to see what you're getting.

212
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:44,063
So that's what we do here.

213
00:08:44,614 --> 00:08:46,734
Now of course, if we swap elements, we now

214
00:08:46,961 --> 00:08:48,888
also need to update our references.

215
00:08:49,645 --> 00:08:50,377
So outerL

216
00:08:50,979 --> 00:08:51,337
is now

217
00:08:52,606 --> 00:08:53,273
result

218
00:08:53,989 --> 00:08:54,249
array

219
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:55,925
outer,

220
00:08:57,477 --> 00:08:58,795
and innerL

221
00:08:59,646 --> 00:09:01,269
is now result array

222
00:09:02,217 --> 00:09:02,506
inner.

223
00:09:04,145 --> 00:09:06,635
Now we're doing this here because I changed

224
00:09:06,635 --> 00:09:08,038
the elements in the outer and inner

225
00:09:08,038 --> 00:09:10,677
position. We swapped them. So now that we

226
00:09:10,757 --> 00:09:11,462
used these

227
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,266
elements stored in our variables

228
00:09:14,843 --> 00:09:17,824
to swap values, we got the right values in

229
00:09:17,824 --> 00:09:19,666
the array, and we can now, on the other

230
00:09:19,666 --> 00:09:22,022
hand, also replace the values stored in our

231
00:09:22,134 --> 00:09:24,938
helper variables here. We need to do that so

232
00:09:24,938 --> 00:09:27,374
that for the next loop iteration, we have

233
00:09:27,598 --> 00:09:29,826
the right values set up, especially for

234
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:32,470
outer l inside of the inner loop here, that

235
00:09:32,470 --> 00:09:34,937
we're operating on the new outer l, which is

236
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:37,021
our swapped value. Again,

237
00:09:37,679 --> 00:09:40,486
you can always console.log these things if

238
00:09:40,486 --> 00:09:42,443
this is a bit too hard to wrap your head

239
00:09:42,443 --> 00:09:42,764
around.

240
00:09:43,631 --> 00:09:45,684
With that, however, we're already done.

241
00:09:46,342 --> 00:09:49,566
Now we go outside of all loops, so here

242
00:09:49,566 --> 00:09:50,898
right before the function ends,

243
00:09:51,476 --> 00:09:53,802
and we simply return our result array. And

244
00:09:53,818 --> 00:09:56,192
that should be the sorted array. Now let's

245
00:09:56,288 --> 00:09:57,973
log it before we analyze it then.

246
00:09:58,871 --> 00:09:59,722
So I'll save that

247
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:01,294
and reload.

248
00:10:01,919 --> 00:10:04,887
And what I get is this array, which looks

